    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) leading our lineup as the premier efficiency plays. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from an elite 25-PA BvP sample against the opposition, which, when combined with a favorable platoon edge against a lefty and a +19% SP skill boost, elevates him into our highest projected tier. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a target for high-ceiling production; his massive +16% park factor adjustment and +14% platoon advantage against a right-handed starter make him an essential anchor in the UTIL spot. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** (78.97) provides our deepest value play, surging due to a massive +19% matchup against the starter, proving that even lower-order hitters provide immense upside when the platoon and pitcher skill metrics align.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Josh Naylor** (52.95) on the bench. Despite a solid projection, he was nudged out by the high-floor utility of **Tyler Soderstrom** and the specific positional requirements of our core. While **Josh Naylor** offers consistent output, his negative park and SP skill adjustments relative to our starters made him the odd man out in a tight efficiency race. We are also closely monitoring the lineup for **Dalton Rushing** and **Gabriel Moreno**, both of whom are projected based on estimated positions; any shifts in their batting order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their respective efficiency scores.\n\nFinally, while we have loaded the lineup for maximum offensive impact, we are cognizant of the defensive risks associated with our speed-focused strategy. Both **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** face elite holding or catching situations that cap their stolen base potential by 1\u20134%, requiring us to rely more on their raw hitting ability than their usual base-stealing upside. **Brice Turang** remains on the bench not only due to lower relative efficiency but also because of a looming 32% rain risk that further diminishes his viability. We remain locked in on optimizing our caps for these high-efficiency matchups to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.",
